From: turbinebmw <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
Subject: media: i2c: vd55g1: add ST VD55G0 support

The VD55G0 (model ID 0x53354730, "S5G0") is the monochrome IR sibling of
the VD55G1 used for Windows Hello on Surface devices: system FSM at 0x002c,
a 552-byte firmware patch applied with BOOT=2 then BOOT=1, one fixed
644x604 RAW10 mode applied verbatim from the Windows tables, and a manual
exposure bank at 0x044x (group hold 0x0448, analogue gain 0x044d, coarse
exposure 0x044e, digital gain 0x0450), mapped to the V4L2 exposure/gain
controls.

Ported to 7.2 from surface-pro-11-linux (patches 0015 and 0017 of the
Surface Pro 11 camera series); still carries that series' bring-up module
parameters (power_hold_ms, scan_on_fail, addr_override, g0_exposure,
g0_again).
